# This package is formatted by hand, not by prettier.
#
# That is a fact found the hard way: `prettier --write` over src/ rewrote 74
# files to prettier's defaults, because no configuration existed and the code
# matched none of them. The diff was three thousand lines of quote characters —
# invisible in review — and it broke scripts/parity.mjs, which reads setting
# names with a regex over single-quoted strings and reported "0/0 settings
# read" afterwards.
#
# No printWidth makes the existing code clean: 100 is closest at 37 files, and
# wider is worse. So there is no configuration to adopt that would make
# `--write` safe here. Until someone reformats the package in one deliberate
# commit, prettier does not touch it.
#
# packages/verification is different — it is prettier-formatted with the
# defaults, and running prettier there is fine.
src
test
